A four-poster bed under a window full of night. It has been a long walk through the dark; the bed is turned down, and SLEEP would end this night kindly. The side door back to the lawn is south.

>sleep
You sleep, mercifully without dreams, and wake to daylight.

>look

Bedchamber
Morning light pours over the old guest bed; for a while, the manor almost forgets itself. The side door back to the lawn is south.

>sleep
You doze through the day, and wake to the window full of night again.

>sleep
You sleep, mercifully without dreams, and wake to daylight.

>south
You step out into the morning, the manor at your back, and the Black Forest, for once, lets you go.
